* loop-stability -- Tian dual-injection loop-gain testbench for ldo_core (issue #10)
*
* Measures the LDO's loop gain T(s) and extracts phase margin / gain margin
* against the ratified stability criterion in
* spec/decision-records/DR-0001-output-cap-strategy.md (PM >= 45 deg AND
* GM >= 10 dB, worst corner, across the full I_load x C_eff x ESR x PVT
* matrix).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Where the loop is broken
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* design/ldo_core.sch deliberately exposes the error-amp output and the
* pass-device gate as two SEPARATE ports (ERRAMP_OUT, PASS_GATE) that are
* unconnected inside the cell, precisely so a stability testbench can break
* the loop there without editing the core (see #8, and the op-point-sanity
* testbench which ties them together for normal operation). This deck
* instantiates the core with those two ports on distinct nodes AINJ / BINJ
* and inserts the injection network between them:
*
*     ERRAMP_OUT (AINJ) --[Vinj]-- (BINJ) PASS_GATE
*                                    |
*                                  [Iinj] (from ground)
*
* AINJ is the DRIVER side (the error amp's output stage, a class-A pfet/nfet
* pair whose small-signal output resistance measures 1/(gds_p+gds_n) ~ 9.3
* MOhm at tt / 27 degC / 3.3 V / 25 mA) and BINJ is the LOAD side (the
* pass-device gate plus the enable-clamp and current-limit clamp gates).
* Vinj is DC 0, so the DC operating point is exactly the closed-loop one --
* no replica bias, no DC loop break, no perturbation of the bias point.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Why dual injection (Tian / Middlebrook), not plain voltage injection
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Plain series-voltage injection is only accurate where Z_load >> Z_source at
* the break. Here Z_source is the amp's ~9 MOhm output resistance and Z_load
* is a few pF of gate capacitance, so that inequality FAILS above roughly
* 1/(2*pi*9Meg*Cgate) ~ a few kHz -- decades below where crossover sits
* (0.8 kHz to 0.24 MHz over the measured matrix).
* Voltage injection alone would therefore report a loop gain that is wrong in
* the decade that decides stability. The Tian/Middlebrook dual-injection
* result is exact regardless of the impedance ratio:
*
*   voltage injection (Vinj ac=1, Iinj ac=0):  Tv = -V(AINJ)/V(BINJ)
*   current injection (Vinj ac=0, Iinj ac=1):  Ti = -I_driver/I_load
*                                                 = -i(Vinj)/(i(Vinj)+1)
*   loop gain:                                 T  = (Tv*Ti - 1)/(Tv + Ti + 2)
*
* With Vinj ac=0 the two nodes are an AC short, so i(Vinj) is the current the
* driver delivers into the junction and i(Vinj)+1 is the current the load
* draws from it (the 1 A phasor being Iinj's injection into BINJ).
*
* T(s) so defined is the loop gain in the T = A*beta sense: positive real at
* DC for this negative-feedback loop, closed-loop suppression 1/(1+T),
* instability at T = -1. Hence
*     phase margin = 180 deg + phase(T) at the 0 dB crossing
*     gain margin  = -|T|dB at the first -180 deg phase crossing.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Gain resurgence above the first 0 dB crossing (issue #59, DR-0008)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Both of those margins are a valid stability test only when T(s) has no
* right-half-plane poles -- the standard precondition on the Bode form of the
* Nyquist criterion. design/error_amp.sch closes a LOCAL loop inside the
* amplifier (the Rz/Cc network around the stage-2 driver and the class-AB gate
* buffer) which stays closed when the LDO loop is broken here, so the
* precondition is a real question, not a formality; DR-0008 records that it
* did not hold for the amplifier as committed at b304bd5.
*
* This deck therefore also measures the cheapest frequency-domain signature of
* that failure: the largest |T| anywhere ABOVE the first 0 dB crossing. For a
* loop whose gain rolls off monotonically through crossover this is negative
* by construction (every point above the crossing is below unity), so any
* positive value means |T| climbs back over unity after having crossed down --
* which is necessary for the misreading DR-0008 documents (crossover taken on
* the far side of a resonance the RHP pair has already rotated +180 deg
* through), though on its own it is NOT sufficient to prove RHP poles.
* sim/amp-selfosc/ remains the load-bearing time-domain measurement.
*
* The scan starts a FIXED 5% above f0 (issue #69) rather than at f0 itself,
* so the crossing point (|T| = 0 dB by definition) cannot be reported as its
* own resurgence. That offset is a stated constant, not a function of the AC
* sweep resolution (AC_DEC) -- see the "gain resurgence" measurement below
* for why, and sim/loop-stability/README.md's "resurgence_db" section for
* the record of the comparability bug this replaces.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Load / output-network model
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* I_load is an ideal DC current source (infinite small-signal impedance).
* That is the standard -- and the conservative -- LDO stability model: a
* resistive load would add 1/gload of damping in parallel with the output
* pole, flattering the result. DR-0001's 0 mA point means "no external load"
* (only the feedback divider's ~6 uA), which this deck models as Iload = 0.
*
* C_eff / ESR are the DERATED effective output capacitance and its ESR at the
* output pin, per DR-0001 -- not a nominal component value.
*
* Template: the at-sign-delimited placeholders below are substituted by
* sweep.py (PDK paths, corner sections, temperature, supply, and the sweep
* lists) before the deck is handed to `ngspice -b`.

.include "@DESIGN_INCLUDE@"
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOS_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @RES_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @BJT_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @DIODE_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOSCAP_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MIMCAP_CORNER@

.temp @TEMP_C@

.include "@LDO_NETLIST@"

* --- stimulus ------------------------------------------------------------
Vin VIN 0 DC @VIN_V@
Ven EN 0 DC @VIN_V@

* --- DUT, loop broken at ERRAMP_OUT -> PASS_GATE --------------------------
* Port order (design/ldo_core.sym / .sch): VIN VOUT EN VSS ERRAMP_OUT PASS_GATE
Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 AINJ BINJ ldo_core

* --- Tian dual-injection network -----------------------------------------
* Vinj is a DC short: the operating point is the true closed-loop one.
Vinj AINJ BINJ DC 0 AC 0
Iinj 0 BINJ DC 0 AC 0

* --- load + output network (swept below; these are the initial values) ----
Iload VOUT 0 DC 0
Resr VOUT NESR 0.001
Cout NESR 0 1e-6

* --- removing the non-physical DC branch ----------------------------------
* An IDEAL current-source load leaves VOUT unbounded below, and that opens a
* second DC solution the Newton solver likes: drive VOUT far negative, and
* the sense leg inside ldo_ilimit sees a permanent overload, clamps
* PASS_GATE to VIN, and the pass device stays off -- self-consistent, so the
* solve stops there. Cold-started, ngspice lands on it at roughly a third of
* the PVT points (e.g. VOUT = -29 V and a DC "loop gain" of -131 dB at
* 10 mA / 0.33 uF / 50 mOhm on tt / 27 degC / 3.3 V), and every margin
* extracted about such a point is meaningless. It is not the closed-loop
* operating point, and it is not a property of the design either: the
* ratified limit is 65-80 mA, sim/current-limit/records/ shows it never
* engages at or below the 50 mA this matrix sweeps, and
* sim/load-regulation/records/ shows the regulating solution exists at every
* corner out to 50 mA. It is an artifact of the ideal load's unbounded range.
*
* .nodeset seeding was tried first and is NOT sufficient -- it fixes some
* corners and leaves others (fs / -40 degC / 2.97 V among them) on the wrong
* branch; so are gmin stepping (`noopiter`), source stepping, an rshunt, a
* transient warm-up, and a load-current continuation sweep. What removes the
* branch is denying it its escape: a diode from ground to VOUT, which does
* nothing until VOUT tries to go below about -0.7 V.
*
* It is inert at the operating point, by construction and by measurement:
*   - reverse-biased by 1.8 V, so its conductance is
*     (IS/n*Vt)*exp(-1.8/n*Vt) ~ 1e-43 S against a 900 kOhm divider;
*   - cjo=0 tt=0, so it contributes no capacitance to the AC solve at all.
*   Measured, over the 51 points of tt / 27 degC / 3.3 V that converge
*   WITHOUT it (the other 21 have no unclamped answer to compare against):
*     VOUT and DC loop gain      identical to every printed digit
*     phase at crossover         identical at 50 of the 51 points; the
*                                remaining one moves by 0.0013 deg
*     crossover frequency        <= 1.7e-5 relative (5th significant figure)
*     gain margin                <= 2.1e-5 relative
*   i.e. it changes which solution is found, not the answer -- the residue
*   is solver round-off, three orders of magnitude below the 0.5 deg budget
*   selftest.py holds the extraction itself to.
*
* sweep.py independently re-checks every row's VOUT against the regulation
* target and voids the run rather than recording margins taken about a bias
* point that is not the regulating one -- so this can never silently stop
* working.
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 cjo=0 tt=0 n=1 rs=0)
Dclamp 0 VOUT dclamp

.control
set noaskquit

echo "* corner_id=@CORNER_ID@ corner=@CORNER_NAME@ temp_c=@TEMP_C@ vin_v=@VIN_V@"
echo "* ac sweep: dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@ ; Tian dual injection at ERRAMP_OUT->PASS_GATE"
echo "* columns: ROW iload_a= ceff_f= esr_ohm= vout_v= dcgain_db= f0_hz= phase_at_f0_deg="
echo "*          f180_hz= gain_at_f180_db= f0_rising_hz= resurgence_db="
echo "* (phase margin = 180 + phase_at_f0_deg ; gain margin = -gain_at_f180_db ;"
echo "*  resurgence_db = max |T| in dB above the first 0 dB crossing, DR-0008 ;"
echo "*  an empty f180/gain field means the phase never reaches -180 deg in band)"
echo "* Fields are written key=value BECAUSE a failed meas leaves its value"
echo "* empty: with bare positional fields an empty one vanishes into the"
echo "* whitespace and every field after it is read as the wrong quantity."

foreach il @ILOAD_LIST@
  foreach ce @CEFF_LIST@
    foreach es @ESR_LIST@
      destroy all
      alter Iload = $il
      alter Cout = $ce
      alter Resr = $es

      * ---- DC operating point (closed loop; Vinj is a DC short) ----------
      op
      let vout_dc = v(vout)
      set vout_str = "$&vout_dc"

      * ---- voltage injection --------------------------------------------
      alter @Vinj[acmag] = 1
      alter @Iinj[acmag] = 0
      ac dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@
      let tv = -v(ainj)/v(binj)
      set vplot = $curplot

      * ---- current injection --------------------------------------------
      alter @Vinj[acmag] = 0
      alter @Iinj[acmag] = 1
      ac dec @AC_DEC@ @F_START@ @F_STOP@
      let ti = -i(vinj)/(i(vinj)+1)
      let tvv = {$vplot}.tv

      * ---- Tian loop gain, magnitude and unwrapped phase -----------------
      let t = (tvv*ti - 1)/(tvv + ti + 2)
      let tdb = db(t)
      let tph = 180*cph(t)/pi

      * ---- margins -------------------------------------------------------
      * A failed `meas` (no such crossing anywhere in the swept band) prints
      * an ngspice error, leaves the variable unset, and the row's field
      * comes out empty -- which sweep.py reads as "no crossing", the
      * physically correct reading for f180/gmx (phase never reaches
      * -180 deg => gain margin is not the limiting criterion). f0r is a
      * self-check: a RISING 0 dB crossing above f0 would mean the gain
      * peaks back over unity and the single-crossover phase-margin reading
      * is not the whole story; sweep.py flags any such point.
      meas ac dcg find tdb at=@F_START@
      meas ac f0 when tdb=0 fall=1
      meas ac phx find tph when tdb=0 fall=1
      meas ac f180 when tph=-180 fall=1
      meas ac gmx find tdb when tph=-180 fall=1
      meas ac f0r when tdb=0 rise=1

      * ---- gain resurgence above the first 0 dB crossing (#59, DR-0008) ---
      * The largest |T| in dB anywhere above the first (falling) 0 dB
      * crossing. The scan starts a FIXED 5% above f0 -- f0*1.05, a constant
      * independent of AC_DEC -- so the crossing itself, where |T| is 0 dB
      * by definition, is not reported as its own resurgence; every
      * remaining point of a monotonically falling |T| is strictly below
      * 0 dB, so the metric is negative unless the gain genuinely climbs
      * back over unity.
      *
      * Issue #69: this offset used to be one AC-grid step (10^(1/AC_DEC)),
      * which ties the metric's VALUE to the sweep resolution even though
      * the quantity it reports -- sup|T| over (f0, F_STOP] -- does not
      * depend on resolution at all. Measured on a byte-identical netlist,
      * AC_DEC 50 -> 400 alone moved resurgence_db at all 4536 matrix
      * points by +0.061...+2.362 dB with phase margin and crossover
      * essentially unmoved (records/20260802-204343-e912fbd.md section 4). A
      * fixed 5% is chosen because it is close to the OLD dec-50 grid step
      * (10^(1/50) ~ 4.71%, the resolution every historical record through
      * 20260802-171044-db620a6 was taken at) -- so this redefinition does
      * not retroactively widen or narrow the scan those records represent
      * -- and it is comfortably above the CURRENT dec-400 grid step
      * (10^(1/400) ~ 0.577%), so no AC_DEC this deck runs at today changes
      * which points the scan considers. selftest.py exercises the
      * resulting invariance directly: the same reference loop measured at
      * two different AC_DEC values must agree to a small, stated
      * tolerance.
      let fres = f0*1.05
      meas ac tres max tdb from=$&fres to=@F_STOP@

      echo "ROW iload_a=$il ceff_f=$ce esr_ohm=$es vout_v=$vout_str dcgain_db=$&dcg f0_hz=$&f0 phase_at_f0_deg=$&phx f180_hz=$&f180 gain_at_f180_db=$&gmx f0_rising_hz=$&f0r resurgence_db=$&tres"
    end
  end
end
echo "* SWEEP COMPLETE @CORNER_ID@"
.endc
.end
